  "name": "AnthroExpo",
  "shortName": "AnEx",
  "description": "AnthroExpo (AnEx) is a hotel-based furry convention in central Oklahoma, run by volunteers of the non-profit Scissortail Fandoms Inc., originally called Our Way Oklahoma. The first edition took place in Oklahoma City in early 2020, and the 2021 edition was held online because of the COVID-19 pandemic. After the 2022 and 2023 editions at the Sheraton Oklahoma City Downtown, it moved to the Embassy Suites in Norman in 2024. In-person attendance has grown every year since 2022, reaching 1,867 in 2026. Each edition has a theme and a charity partner, and the mascots are Andrea the Scissortail Flycatcher and Exavier the Prairie Dog. The 2027 edition moves from early February to Memorial Day weekend because of hotel renovations.",
